# Waivers for `oasdiff breaking` (just contracts-check / the contracts CI job).
#
# One waived change per line. oasdiff ignores a breaking change when a line
# here contains both its endpoint ("POST /tasks") and its description, matched
# case-insensitively as substrings; any other line is inert, so '#' lines
# serve as comments.
# Every waiver states why the change is safe and when to remove the line —
# the same rule as the CVE waivers in .grype.yaml / osv-scanner.toml.
#
# Remove once master carries the pattern (the diff against the base then
# disappears and the line is dead). Safe because the store never accepted a NUL
# title: before the pattern such requests failed with 500, so no client relied
# on them — the pattern documents behaviour, it does not narrow it.
POST /tasks added the pattern `^[^\u0000]+$` to the request property `title`
